>
    <article class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
        <h1>About ShedOS</h1>

        <p>
            ShedOS is an operating system for software developers. It ships a
            tiling Hyprland desktop and a full development environment, already
            configured, and it treats the machine as something you can change
            freely and always take back.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it exists</h2>

        <p>
            A workstation should be ready the moment it boots, keep the
            configuration you give it, and recover when something goes wrong.
            ShedOS is built so that it does. The desktop and toolchain come
            configured. Your edits survive upgrades. Every upgrade is a
            snapshot you can roll back in one command, and a system that fails
            to reach the desktop several times in a row returns to the last
            working snapshot on its own.
        </p>

        <h2>What's in the box</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>A tiling Hyprland desktop on Wayland — waybar, mako, walker, and a themed lock screen.</li>
            <li>Neovim (LazyVim), VS Code, and Zsh, configured.</li>
            <li>Language runtimes for Python, Node, Go, Rust, and C++.</li>
            <li>Docker and Kubernetes tooling — kubectl, minikube, and helm.</li>
            <li>A Btrfs root with automatic snapshots; LUKS encryption optional at install time.</li>
            <li><code>shedman</code> — one command-line tool for updates, rollback, configuration, theming, and more.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Source and license</h2>

        <p>
